Z||000003||erikred||05-07-2001||12:53 PM||||That was probably me. Someone on this list claims to have a 153 crank in the 151 block. I tend to believe him. The 153 and 181 are the same motor. The 151 is the result of pontiac making their changes to the block for FWD and calling it theirs. I have talked to someone recently who claims to have used marine parts in his S10 motor. He is sending me pictures of the parts. I plan on buying them and finding out for sure.||||reg||10
Z||000004||Raydar||05-07-2001||01:21 PM||||Erikred, <BR>The first I ever heard about the marine crank was on the newsgroup, a couple of days ago. This is of particular interest to me.<BR>I have an 88 Duke that I have been planning to replace with a 2.8. (Got a parts car really cheap.) If I can put the 153 crank in it and make it "walk and talk", I think it would be a neat trick. <BR>Please let us know what you find out. <BR>BTW... <BR>Erikred and Modifie, welcome to the Forum!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
