Z||000007||MODIFIE||05-08-2001||06:09 AM||||erikred I have the info on the 153 crank build, I well put it up on the site in the mods list <A HREF="http://www.dukemods.50megs.com/PAGE1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.dukemods.50megs.com/PAGE1.html</A> <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by erikred:<BR><B>That was probably me. Someone on this list claims to have a 153 crank in the 151 block. I tend to believe him. The 153 and 181 are the same motor. The 151 is the result of pontiac making their changes to the block for FWD and calling it theirs. I have talked to someone recently who claims to have used marine parts in his S10 motor. He is sending me pictures of the parts. I plan on buying them and finding out for sure.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||12
Z||000008||mrossum||05-08-2001||09:16 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by erikred:<BR><B>Someone on this list claims to have a 153 crank in the 151 block.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>i have the 153 crank in my engine. the short block it completely together, but am having valve train geometry issues right now. when i get them figured out, the rest of engine can go together. also have a built th440 trans to go in car. will keep you all posted.||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrossum||05-08-2001||09:25 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B>If I can put the 153 crank in it and make it "walk and talk", I think it would be a neat trick</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>the 153 crank won't work in your 88 engine. 88 is a distributorless engine, and uses a sensor on side of block the reads crank position from ring on crank. there is no place to put ring on 153 crank.||||reg||9
Z||000010||erikred||05-08-2001||10:23 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrossum:<BR><B> the 153 crank won't work in your 88 engine. 88 is a distributorless engine, and uses a sensor on side of block the reads crank position from ring on crank. there is no place to put ring on 153 crank.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The 88 crank also has an internal balancer built in to it. My 88 ran really smooth. I am trying to decide what degree of build up to do to it. If I go wild I will probably need to discontinue the computer controls and  go with a carb and distributor. I may just goahead and find out how much the stock crank can handle and build a seperate stroker motor for later.<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000011||Raydar||05-08-2001||12:59 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrossum:<BR><B> the 153 crank won't work in your 88 engine. 88 is a distributorless engine, and uses a sensor on side of block the reads crank position from ring on crank. there is no place to put ring on 153 crank.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>DOH!!! <BR>Of course, you're right! Forgot about the DIS, completely.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>That's okay. This is the most interesting Duke mod that I've heard of in a while. <BR>Waiting to hear how it works out.<P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
