Z||000013||Cozmo||05-09-2001||09:43 AM||||When digging around on the history of this engine, I found out that GM sold rights of manufacture to Jeep.  They modified it for  a MPFI head and got 123 HP out of it. <A HREF="http://www.off-road.com/jeep/tech/engine/amc150.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.off-road.com/jeep/tech/engine/amc150.html</A> <BR>Don't know how much stuff from this engine we can use, but it's worth looking into...<BR><B>C02M0</B>||||reg||1
Z||000014||84Bill||05-09-2001||10:44 AM||||Woohoo gotta go check this out!||||reg||14
Z||000015||erikred||05-09-2001||11:26 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cozmo:<BR><B>When digging around on the history of this engine, I found out that GM sold rights of manufacture to Jeep.  They modified it for  a MPFI head and got 123 HP out of it. <A HREF="http://www.off-road.com/jeep/tech/engine/amc150.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.off-road.com/jeep/tech/engine/amc150.html</A> <BR>Don't know how much stuff from this engine we can use, but it's worth looking into...<BR>[b]C02M0</B>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I believe the engine you refer to is an AMC engine and not the same as the GM 2.5.||||reg||12
